course: dictionary
lesson: 3468
title: Faith: trust, religion, and phrases
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Faith means a strong trust or belief in someone or something, even when you have no proof. «She kept faith in her best friend, even when everyone else doubted him.» Nobody had proved he was innocent, so her faith was trust without proof.
explain: A faith, with an a and often an s, means a religion. «People of all faiths were invited to the school's winter fair.» Here faiths means religions, such as Christianity, Islam, Judaism, Hinduism, Sikhism or Buddhism. So the little word a tells you it is a religion, not a feeling.
explain: Faith also appears in phrases. «He had lost faith in the team after five defeats» means he no longer trusted them. «She acted in good faith» means she acted honestly. When you meet faith in a phrase, learn the whole phrase as one chunk and check it against the sentence.
fact: Faith means strong trust or belief, even without proof.
fact: A faith is a religion, such as Sikhism or Buddhism.
fact: Faith can also mean belief in God or gods.
fact: «Lose faith» means stop trusting someone or something. «Keep the faith» means keep believing.
fact: «In good faith» means honestly, meaning you truly meant well.
exercise: «The team had lost faith in their coach after three defeats.» What does lost faith mean? | They started a new religion | *They no longer trusted their coach | They all went home early | They gave their coach a present
exercise: Miss Ali says, «Children of all faiths are welcome here.» What does faiths mean? | Sports teams | Shops | Holidays | *Religions
exercise: «Her faith gave her comfort when she was sad.» What does faith mean here? | *Belief in God | A football match | A shop that sells books | A type of cake
test: «He acted in good faith, and everyone believed him.» What does in good faith mean? | Angrily | Secretly | Quickly | *Honestly
test: Which of these is a faith? | Patience | Courage | *Hinduism | Trust
exam: Ravi says, «I will keep the faith, even when the match looks lost.» What does keep the faith mean? | Keep the money safe | Stop playing and go home | *Keep trusting and believing | Forget about the match
